(d) Legitimate aim: Did the interference serve a legitimate aim under Art 11(2)? The mayor claimed it would "create conditions for breaches of the public order". Public order is a legitimate aim. So the aim is public order. The question is whether the aim is indeed legitimate. The law permits restriction to protect public order. So yes, the aim is legitimate.

